WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
- There is a chance that
COVID-19 was created in a lab.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.527
And then it leaked out
and infected the world.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:07.770
- [Lady News Reporter] Chinese city,

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.240
where the coronavirus pandemic

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.910
is believed to have started...

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.020
- A very competent,
trustworthy scientists.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.630
- Probably it was incompetent.
Somebody was stupid.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.040
- Whoa. Did I just say that?

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.240
Yes, I did.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.690
Six months ago, I would not
have been able to say that

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.160
but today I can and we
need to talk about it.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.840
Humans, including myself,
hate uncertainty, ambiguity.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.600
We want to know what happened
but in the case of COVID-19,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.140
we still don't know exactly what happened.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:37.600
We don't know where it came from.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.690
And to try to get at the real answer,

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.520
you have to navigate
all sorts of politics,

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.960
but wait, isn't this a science question?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.030
Isn't it a matter of epidemiology?

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.460
The origin of a virus?

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.830
It should be but woven into
this scientific question

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.410
are a bunch of heavy political questions

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.950
and considerations that are influencing

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.120
what kind of questions
we're allowed to ask

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.130
and what kind of answers
we're allowed to give.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:06.180
So, I wanna strip away the
politics, the tension with China,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.930
the idea that this all sounds
like one big conspiracy

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:12.960
and I wanna just look at the
evidence of one question,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.950
which is, where did COVID-19 come from?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.570
- [Narrator] The most trafficked
wild animal in the world.

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.500
- Wuhan also has China's only bio-safety

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.530
level four super laboratory.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:24.943
- China has a history of lab accidents.

00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:25.776
(suspenseful music)

00:01:25.776 --> 00:01:28.500
Are you suggesting that
maybe you have some evidence

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.350
that this was not a
naturally occurring virus?

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.290
- So it's not just me who wants
to know the answer to this.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.760
Last month president Biden

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.210
asked the U.S intelligence community

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.880
to double down in answering
this one question,

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.190
where did COVID come from?

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.070
- It's important to
know the answer to that.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.860
Right now, there are two major hypotheses,

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.443
one is the spillover hypothesis

00:01:48.443 --> 00:01:51.210
and the second one is
the lab leak hypothesis,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.900
which has up until recently

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.310
been seen as a fringe conspiracy theory.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:56.567
- Complete baloney.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:59.070
- And I'm gonna explain why
that changed in just a minute

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.860
but first let's look at each of these.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:02.840
First, the spillover hypothesis.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.360
- Health officials believe
COVID-19 originated in animals,

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.443
sold in a so-called wet market in China.

00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:10.940
- Pangolin kissed the turtle.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:11.930
(audience laughing)

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.990
- The spillover hypothesis says that

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.850
the coronavirus came from bats in China,

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.140
which is pretty predictable.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.300
Bat's in China have tons of
corona viruses all the time.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.430
They're usually not infectious to humans

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.430
but the hypothesis says
that a strain came about

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.250
that was infectious to maybe an animal,

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.830
maybe one of these guys, a pangolin.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.860
And then that animal showed
up in some supply chain,

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.860
some market in central China

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.830
and it came in contact with the human

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.750
and the human got COVID-19.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.880
And in fact, for a while, it
was this particular market

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.530
in Wu Han that was seen as the culprit.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.580
They thought the bat
virus was in an animal

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.010
somewhere in this market.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.280
And now listen for a really long time

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.500
up until just recently, I didn't
know this was a hypothesis,

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.110
I thought this was a fact.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.410
In the early days of the pandemic,

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.680
they would talk about this
like it wasn't a question,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.040
they'd be like, and the virus that came

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.139
from this meat market.

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:05.060
- The virus originated from a market.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.240
- [Male Reporter] This meat market,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.730
Ground Zero for the outbreak.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:11.430
- But guess what? There's
no direct evidence for this.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.140
They don't even have pangolin
in the Wu Han wet market.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.290
And soon we learned that the
first official COVID case

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.060
had no contact with this market.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.930
So the Chinese CDC had
to come out and say,

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.830
okay, no, it actually has
nothing to do with this market,

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.120
we have no idea where
this outbreak came from

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.170
but even after they said

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.670
that the market wasn't the epicenter,

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.770
the idea was still that
this came from a bat

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.390
that transferred it to an animal,

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.810
that transferred it to a human,

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.600
the spillover hypothesis.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.990
The main reason why this
hypothesis gained so much traction

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.570
was because this is how
pandemics usually happen.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.520
Of the past five pandemics,

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.940
four of them were the result of a virus

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.060
jumping from an animal onto humans.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.670
So even though no one had
found an animal with COVID-19

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.160
to prove this theory,

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.370
they sort of presumed that it had to be

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.080
because look at these other four,

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.860
but wait, what about this one?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.730
The Russian flu of 1977,

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.350
was likely the result of a lab accident.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.270
And it ended up killing
hundreds of thousands of people

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:13.415
but even still the spillover
hypothesis was kind of gospel.

00:04:13.415 --> 00:04:14.990
(suspenseful music)

