00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.550
But quietly, there was another theory

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.250
that was brewing under the surface.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.110
One that many experts
didn't talk about publicly

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.960
at the time, but they thought about.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.280
They were thinking of
another building in Wuhan,

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.940
not this market, but another building

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.090
that was just a few miles down the road,

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.770
this one right here, the
Wuhan Institute Of Virology.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:56.050
- So here's, what's crazy.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.150
It's exactly in this lab in Wuhan,

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:01.190
where scientists have been experimenting

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.130
for years with corona viruses,

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:06.670
engineering them to make
them even more infectious

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.010
to human beings.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.840
- More infectious to humans?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:13.880
Wow! By the way, that's Podgy,
he's one of my producers.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.250
He reached out to me a while back

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:18.220
and said that we should look
into the alternative hypothesis

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:19.850
of where COVID came from,

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.090
including this idea that it
may have leaked from this lab.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.920
At the time I was quite skeptical,

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.170
I had heard rumblings about
the idea of the lab accident

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.340
that caused COVID and I'd
sort of written it off

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.580
because it just seemed so conspiracy

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.900
like just like low hanging for conspiracy,

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.210
like super engineered
virus escapes from lab

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.740
and starts global pandemic.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.640
It's like new world orders.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:46.030
It just reeks of internet
conspiracy and disinformation.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.160
And in addition to that,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.330
the only people who were touting this

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:52.460
were like people who are
not very good at the truth

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.300
and people who also liked
to pick fights with China.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.133
- I can tell you that

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.720
there is a significant amount of evidence

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.620
that this came from that
laboratory in Wuhan.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:04.130
- But I told Podgy that
if there's any evidence,

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.690
even circumstantial that
warrants looking further

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.950
into this hypothesis,
I would be interested

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.600
in checking it out.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:16.600
And it turns out there was
such evidence and here it goes.

00:07:16.961 --> 00:07:20.000
(lively music)

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.430
So, this is the lab leak hypothesis,

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.400
and I'm gonna unpack it the best I can.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.570
First, let's talk about this lab.

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.010
It's located in central
China in the city of Wuhan

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.250
and for years, they
have been experimenting

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.380
on corona viruses what
Podgy was telling me about.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.800
The question is, why
on earth would you want

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.920
to make a coronavirus
more infectious to humans?

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.350
- So this is what's known
as, gain of function research

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.840
and the idea is to study
more infectious versions

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.770
of the virus in order to
learn from that what we need

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.580
in order to stop the next pandemic

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.900
from ever happening in the first place.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.977
- Gain of function research.

00:07:53.977 --> 00:07:56.100
This is sort of like
testing nuclear weapons.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.850
You're sort of playing with fire,

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.490
testing something that has the power

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.690
to kill millions of
people but you're doing so

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.910
in the name of like helping humanity.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.370
There are only three places on earth

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:07.240
that do this sort of risky research

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:10.050
and it's supposed to be done
in these super high security

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.360
bio secure facilities that
have all these parameters

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.490
to make sure that the
engineered virus doesn't escape.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:18.410
And by the way, in the
scientific community,

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.610
many people think this is
too risky and not worth it.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.537
One critique I read from a
scientific journal said that,

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:28.230
"If the virus escapes, nobody
could predict the trajectory."

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.600
We're messing with
genetics and that's scary.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.920
Okay, but just to remember for a second,

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:34.170
that all of this gain of function research

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.873
is happening in like 2015 through 2018.

00:08:38.778 --> 00:08:40.830
Just rewind for a second.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.800
None of us had heard the
word coronavirus before.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.430
This was effectively some
boring, wonky, nerdy debate

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.160
happening between super niche scientists

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.360
who were studying the best
way to look at viruses

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.420
and all the while, as they did work,

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.650
studying all of these
corona viruses from bats,

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:02.330
the freezers in this lab
in Wuhan started filling up

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.130
with more and more samples of
corona viruses of all kinds.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:08.040
Some just captured from bats and caves

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.330
and others engineered to be
more infectious to humans.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.650
But again, no one really cared.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.160
If I had made a video
about this work in 2017,

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.460
you wouldn't have watched it.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.250
But in 2017, there was
someone who did care,

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.570
it was someone at the
U.S embassy in Beijing.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.760
They caught wind that in this Wuhan lab,

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.750
they were curating corona viruses

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.990
and engineering more infectious ones.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.080
This wasn't some secret,

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:33.060
this was like in
collaboration with scientists

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:34.440
in the U.S and around the world.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.050
But even still, they sent
a team of health experts

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:40.640
to check out the lab and
what they saw troubled them.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.490
The lab wasn't nearly as
safe as it needed to be.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.340
And the managers at the lab said that

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:47.110
they were lobbying for more resources

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.770
so that they could hire
properly trained technicians

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.370
to safely run the lab.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.800
The diplomats were concerned

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.320
and they sent two messages
back to Washington, DC

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.220
at two different periods of time.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.860
They said this lab isn't safe

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.330
and the state department
should work with the Chinese

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.800
to tighten security.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.020
These two cables went
back to Washington, DC

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.630
and both were ignored.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:11.080
Again, this was like super
boring stuff in 2017 and 2018,

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.003
no one had heard of Anthony Fowchee,

00:10:13.003 --> 00:10:15.210
this wasn't top priority.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.330
So it was ignored, until 2020

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.700
when suddenly we all care about virology.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.030
- Concerns about the deadly coronavirus,

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:25.846
officially getting the U.S.

00:10:25.846 --> 00:10:29.600
(suspenseful music)

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.080
- Okay, so you have this lab

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.110
that's doing gain of function research,

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.380
there may be not very secure.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.140
Now it's 2020, and I
need to explain something

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.400
that was hard for me
to understand at first

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:41.680
but it's very important.

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:44.700
Any hypothesis as to the origins of COVID

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.180
has to take into account

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:51.060
the fact that this new deadly
coronavirus called COVID-19

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.600
broke out in the very city

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.270
where the largest repository
of coronavirus samples

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.620
sit in a freezer in this lab,

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.009
some of which have been engineered

00:11:02.009 --> 00:11:02.842
to become more infectious to humans.

00:11:02.842 --> 00:11:05.540
Oh, in the lab has been
deemed not super safe.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.670
If the outbreak had
happened in some other city

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.250
where there was no lab with a freezer

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.880
full of corona viruses,

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.580
we would not be having this conversation,

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.070
this would not even be on the table,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.960
but Wuhan is the epicenter of
coronavirus samples on earth

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.380
because of this lab-

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.850
- Oh my God! There's been an outbreak

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:27.890
of chocolatey goodness,
near Hershey, Pennsylvania.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.150
What do you think happened?

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:30.550
Like, oh, I don't know.

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:34.340
Maybe a steam shovel
mated with a cocoa bean

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:37.428
or it's the (beep) chocolate factory.

00:11:37.428 --> 00:11:38.510
(audience laughs)

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.343
- Okay, wait, wait, hold on

00:11:39.343 --> 00:11:40.320
I know some of you were thinking this,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.290
I was thinking this,

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.480
at first, I thought this
was a logical fallacy.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.380
Originally, I had said, well, of course,

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:48.450
it's not a coincidence that
there's a coronavirus lab

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.200
in the same city, that
there was an outbreak.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.740
The lab was probably set up

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:54.550
because there's a lot of corona viruses

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:56.230
so they set up the lab to study it

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.690
so that they could prevent it
but then I read an interview

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:02.150
with one of the top researchers

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:05.610
at the Wuhan lab, one of
the biggest experts in bats

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.543
and corona viruses and
this changed my mind.

00:12:08.543 --> 00:12:11.126
(upbeat music)

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:14.320
Her name is Shi Zhengli

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:17.023
but her nickname is, 'The bat woman.'

00:12:17.023 --> 00:12:20.161
(crushing noises)

00:12:20.161 --> 00:12:21.830
- You're about to become compost.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.770
- Because she's made her
career out of going into caves,

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.780
getting coronavirus samples from bats,

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.090
so that she can study them.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:29.970
She's like a top expert on this stuff

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.670
and she works in the Wuhan lab.

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.270
When she heard that there
was a coronavirus outbreak

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.800
in Wuhan, she was in
Shanghai at a conference,

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.340
so she got on a train
to rush back to Wuhan

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:43.017
so she's on this train and
later she said in an interview,

00:12:43.017 --> 00:12:46.830
"I wondered if the local
health authorities got it wrong

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.560
by calling it the coronavirus."

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.250
She's like, something's off here.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.840
Wuhan is in central China

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.350
and from the bat woman's
extensive study into this

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:59.330
she knows that it's
actually Southern China,

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.490
where all the bats are and
where coronavirus is most likely

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.440
to jump from animals to humans.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.060
We're down here in Southern China

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.840
that's where COVID-19
cousin SARS broke out

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.900
in the early 2000, that's the place

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:14.890
where there is an actual
major risk of coronavirus

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:15.730
jumping from animals.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.710
So the bat woman is on this
train, shaking her head,

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.657
she literally said in the interview,

00:13:20.657 --> 00:13:23.540
"I had never expected this
kind of thing to happen

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.940
in Wuhan, in central China."

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.410
This is a thing that
happens in Southern China,

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.620
not Central China.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:32.297
And then the terrifying
thought hit her, she said,

00:13:32.297 --> 00:13:35.220
"Could they have come from our lab?"

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:39.160
Her first thought was the
health officials got this wrong,

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:41.910
it's either not coronavirus or if it is,

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.660
it probably came from our lab,

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.180
that's the more likely scenario,

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.840
not that it jumped from animals
like it does southern China.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.820
So no, the lab isn't set up in Wuhan

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.130
because Wuhan is the
epicenter of corona viruses

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.010
jumping from animals,
instead Wuhan's relationship

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:58.510
to corona viruses isn't that it's common,

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:00.270
that it breaks out in wet markets,

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.220
no, it's because of the lab.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.580
The lab is the world's largest sample

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:06.020
of corona viruses on earth.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:08.150
Now, let's be clear this isn't part proof

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:10.250
that anything happened,
this is circumstantial

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:14.060
but it is absolutely a firm
foundation for a hypothesis

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.660
that potentially this
could have come from a lab

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.740
bat woman herself, that
was her first thought.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.550
And as I've been reading the
accounts from other virologists

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.300
and epidemiologists around the world

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.150
who heard of a virus coming out of Wuhan,

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.270
they thought about the lab.

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:28.210
They're like, oh, shit
there's a giant lab there

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:31.300
with tons of viruses, I
wonder if it came from there.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.120
Now, listen, this lady who
we're calling, bat woman,

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:37.270
the bat expert, went to the
lab as soon as she got to Wuhan

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.510
she was sort of freaking out.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:39.960
She had been losing sleep.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.160
And she looked at all of
the data, all of the samples

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.300
and determined that none
of the samples engineered

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.860
or natural were the same as COVID-19.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.410
None of them were an exact match

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.880
and she sighed a breath of relief

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:53.260
and she felt like,
okay, it wasn't our lab.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.200
For most scientists, that was enough proof

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.410
to put the lab leak hypothesis to rest.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.380
They're like, oh yeah,
bat woman said that,

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.690
none of the samples were
identical to COVID-19

00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:05.460
but for many others,
trusting this one woman

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:06.620
to tell us the truth

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.650
or to have done a thorough investigation

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:11.780
is not good enough evidence
for us to rule this out.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:15.150
The world who has suffered
greatly because of COVID-19,

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:18.330
deserves a chance to truly investigate

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.170
not trust one Chinese researcher.

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.820
- The world has reached
another grim milestone

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:25.900
in the history of the
coronavirus pandemic.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.780
- This is globally the
death toll has now topped

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.420
a staggering 3 million people.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:32.650
- But for some reason,

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:35.990
China is not really playing
ball with letting an inquiry

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.330
or an investigation happen.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.450
When Australia got up

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.450
and called for a transparent investigation

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.770
into COVID origins,

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.460
including looking into
the lab leak hypothesis,

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:48.500
China immediately retaliated
with economic sanctions

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.220
on Australian products like wine and beef.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.672
What?

00:15:52.672 --> 00:15:53.510
A little defensive.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.410
Like wouldn't China want to have

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.730
an independent investigation
into this hypothesis

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:00.110
so that if it's false,
it can be proven false

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:01.820
and we can put it to rest.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:03.830
It seems like that would
be in their interest

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:06.130
and yet they're making
it incredibly difficult

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.270
for anyone to do an investigation.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.900
Instead, we have to rely
on U.S spies and intel

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.410
to like piece this together.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.180
The Wall Street Journal recently reported

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.860
that there was intel that said that,

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:20.090
three researchers at
the Wuhan lab got sick

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:21.900
with COVID like symptoms

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:25.570
and they had to be
hospitalized in November 2019,

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:28.470
weeks before the first
official case of COVID.

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:30.050
Again, this isn't proof

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.850
but it's definitely reason
to ask more questions.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:36.630
China, stop making us
rely on intel from spies,

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:40.250
put the hypothesis to bed
and let us investigate

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.220
but they won't, which is
like incredibly suspicious.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.610
- Mike at the end of the day,

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:47.220
it's profoundly in China's
interest to do this as well

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:50.260
because look, it's suffered too.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.220
- That's the lab leak
hypothesis, unsafe lab,

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:55.190
that's the coronavirus epicenter

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:58.630
and an engineer's viruses to
be more infectious for humans

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.910
has a little mishap, which
turns into a global pandemic.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.790
It's a feasible hypothesis
that deserves investigation.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.660
Now, listen, if your brain
is anything like my brain,

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.780
what both of our brains
are doing right now,

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.530
is scheming to find
some sort of certainty,

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.210
we're like, oh, look at
all this evidence here.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.470
They were in the hospital

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.650
and Wuhan is actually the epicenter

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.380
and we're like piecing it all together.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.000
Our brains love to do this,

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.320
to lay out the circumstances
and fill in the blanks

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:27.100
so that we can believe in
some sort of certain thing,

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.100
our brains hate ambiguity

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:32.080
but please don't be tricked
by your hate for ambiguity.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.142
We have to remember that
neither the spillover hypothesis

00:17:35.142 --> 00:17:39.610
nor the lab leak hypothesis
have solid direct evidence

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.610
that proved them one way or the other.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.444
The main evidence for the
spillover hypothesis right now

00:17:44.444 --> 00:17:46.540
is the idea that historically,

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.950
this is how viruses like to start,

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.820
they jump from animals onto humans.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.260
That's a really solid
basis for our hypothesis.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.750
We should absolutely
continue to investigate that.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:56.583
But guess what?

00:17:56.583 --> 00:17:59.390
It's been a year and a half
and we haven't found an animal

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.660
who carries COVID after a year and a half?

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:05.100
So as of now, it is still in
the category of hypothesis

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.430
but if you read the news in 2020,

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:11.110
it seemed like the case was
closed, it was a settled thing,

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:13.480
yeah, the coronavirus
jumped from an animal.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.526
- The pangolin.

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:15.359
- Pangolin.

00:18:15.359 --> 00:18:16.192
- Pangolins.

00:18:16.192 --> 00:18:17.025
- Probably one of these
pangolins in a market,

00:18:17.025 --> 00:18:18.150
everyone move on.

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:21.860
Meanwhile, the lab leak
hypothesis also had solid basis.

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.810
None of the evidence I've
talked about today is new,

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:25.430
it's all been around.

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.880
And yet until recently
the idea of a lab accident

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.940
being the origins of COVID-19,

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:35.230
was deemed as far off fringe conspiracy.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.663
- This question about the Wuhan lab,

00:18:37.663 --> 00:18:39.370
we know that it's been debunked

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:41.910
that this virus was manmade or modified.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:42.810
- A major reason for that

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:45.000
was because there was
the Trump administration

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.580
that was constantly
overstating the hypothesis,

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:50.000
claiming they had way more
evidence than they actually did,

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.040
labeling it, the China virus.

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.560
- The Chinese virus.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:57.440
It's not racist at all, no, not
at all, it comes from China.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.530
- Which helped fuel a
spike in discrimination

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:02.350
and violence against people
of East Asian descent.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:05.080
And then Tom Cotton
gets up and says, this-

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.810
- The virus went into that food market

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.570
before it came out of that food market.

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:10.140
So we don't know where it originated

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.830
but we do know that we have
to get to the bottom of that.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.890
We also know that just a few miles away

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.700
from that food market is China's only

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:20.240
bio-safety level four super laboratory

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.460
that researches human infectious diseases.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:25.320
- Well, this is awkward.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:26.170
Yeah.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:28.790
It turns out what Tom Cotton said,

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.120
actually is totally sensible.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:33.080
I had written this into the script,

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.020
thinking that Tom Cotton

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.530
said some crazy stuff about something.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:40.830
- What 5G actually does, it absorbs oxygen

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.740
and that's really important know.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.350
- But it turns out that Tom Cotton

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:49.350
back in like February of
2020 was stating a hypothesis

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:53.023
that a bunch of scientists
now think is totally legit.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.310
Nothing's changed, we
don't have any new evidence

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:58.140
and yet at the time it was written off

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.360
as a total fringe conspiracy.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.193
Here's the New York Times,

00:20:01.193 --> 00:20:03.590
Senator Tom Cotton repeats fringe theory

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.320
on coronavirus origins.

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:08.040
It was completely downplayed, written off

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.870
and put aside as a fringe conspiracy.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.090
This was a failure of journalism

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:16.610
and journalism's job of
looking into hypothesis

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:20.050
and actually validating them
based on the available evidence

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:22.720
as Tom cotton says, "There actually wasn't

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.760
any direct evidence
and there still isn't."

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.010
And yet today nothing has changed

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:28.950
but scientists look at the hypothesis

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.870
and see it as totally legit
and worthy of investigating.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.590
And I almost just got
caught in the pitfall,

00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:37.450
trying to do journalism
and about to regurgitate

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:40.320
what I read on the Washington
Post and New York Times

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:42.410
that Tom Cotton said some crazy stuff,

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:43.550
when he actually didn't.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.440
That is dangerous, when
reporters just repeat

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:49.380
what others are and jump on the bandwagon

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:51.630
because it's correct to do that.

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:55.210
What's correct is to go report
and look into the evidence,

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.890
which is something that a
lot of journalists didn't do

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:58.010
during this time.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:21:00.210
And so scientists, even if they believe

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:03.970
that we should investigate it
and the media downplayed it,

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.607
wouldn't touch it until recently.

00:21:06.607 --> 00:21:08.910
- Now the coronavirus may have leaked

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.037
from a lab in Wuhan China.

00:21:10.037 --> 00:21:11.290
- [Lady News Reporter]
U.S president Joe Biden

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.420
launched the investigation in late May.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:17.800
- Why would you have a bad
coronavirus outbreak in Wuhan

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.170
and not in Southern China

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.490
where these horseshoe bats are located?

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.480
- Trump left office
and things settled down

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:24.480
with China a little bit.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:27.370
And lo and behold, we're
now seeing legitimate,

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.720
well-respected experts on
this topic come out publicly

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.120
and declare that the lab leak
hypothesis isn't a conspiracy

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.040
and that both hypotheses
need to be taken seriously

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:40.400
until we have sufficient data.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:43.080
It's called science, by the
way, it's just called science,

00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:45.170
should look into legitimate hypothesis.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.200
But what was troubling
to me is that even still,

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:50.170
there are scientists who
are digging in their heels

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:51.730
saying that the case is closed.

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:54.500
- There is zero evidence that this virus

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.700
came out of the lab in China.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.150
- Like this guy, for example,

00:21:57.150 --> 00:22:00.850
he's a leading expert in animal
diseases and disease ecology

00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:04.010
and he's been the leader of
calling the lab leak hypothesis,

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:07.340
a fringe conspiracy theory,
like since the beginning,

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.320
when we knew nothing,
but here's the thing,

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.900
this guy has skin in the game.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:15.390
His NGO gets loads of funding
to perform research at,

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:18.050
wait for it, the Wuhan lab.

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:19.630
- [Male Reporter] Members
of the scientific community

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:22.070
have said that Daszak has
a conflict of interest

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:25.710
due to his close ties to the
Wuhan Institute of Virology

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:27.837
and its leading scientist, Shi Zhengli.

00:22:27.837 --> 00:22:29.810
- Yes of course, he
doesn't want the Wuhan lab

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:33.090
or gain of function
research to be smeared,

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:35.690
like this is his home
turf where his livelihood

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:37.480
and his life's work comes from.

00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:39.130
And he's the guy we're listening to?

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:41.960
Like we're letting this
guy lead out on the inquiry

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:45.237
about where the origins
of COVID come from?

00:22:45.237 --> 00:22:48.237
(suspenseful music)

00:22:53.319 --> 00:22:54.400
Oh and it gets worse.

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:56.790
So the WHO, World Health Organization

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:59.380
sent a group to investigate
the origins of COVID

00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:02.460
a few months ago and this
guy helped lead the team.

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:04.520
I mean, he's like a world
expert, but guess what?

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:07.530
The results of what he came
back with, were not surprising.

00:23:07.530 --> 00:23:09.100
- A team Of international experts

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:11.430
investigating the origins of COVID-19

00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:13.640
have all but dismissed a theory

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:15.140
that the virus came from a lab.

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:17.370
- And talk to people,
ask critical questions,

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:20.510
got critical answers and
they've come to their conclusion

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:24.010
and I have as well and what
they say is extremely unlikely.

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:25.920
- But then eventually a
journalist calls him out.

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:28.400
- Given that this report
rules out of that leak,

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:30.570
isn't your credibility on
that a little undermined

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:32.150
by the fact that you've been saying that

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:34.380
even before you came here?

00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:35.213
- No.

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:36.960
- Yes, you can't go into an investigation

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.070
with your mind already made up dude!

00:23:39.070 --> 00:23:41.460
Especially when millions
of dollars of funding

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:43.670
for your organization is on the line,

00:23:43.670 --> 00:23:47.370
that's not science that's
self-interest and tribalism.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:48.790
Listen, I don't doubt that Daszak

00:23:48.790 --> 00:23:52.540
is an earnest believer in his theory,

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.940
I mean, he's a zoologist by training

00:23:54.940 --> 00:23:57.020
of course he thinks it jumped from animals

00:23:57.020 --> 00:23:59.560
but this shouldn't be the
guy doing the investigation.

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:01.900
Oh, and it's not just me who
thinks that this investigation

00:24:01.900 --> 00:24:06.410
was BS, the head of the
WHO, literally the head

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.700
who commissioned this study said that

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.407
the investigation into
the lab leak theory,

00:24:11.407 --> 00:24:13.550
"wasn't extensive enough."

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:14.430
It was too hasty.

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:16.183
So yeah, they didn't
actually look into it.

00:24:16.183 --> 00:24:19.530
This scientists are not
actually looking earnestly

00:24:19.530 --> 00:24:20.600
for empirical evidence.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:24.030
Okay, that was a lot. there's
a lot to soak in here.

00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:25.920
And I wanna give you a few big takeaways

00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:28.800
that are like nothing we should
take away from this video.

00:24:28.800 --> 00:24:31.070
Number one is that, we don't know,

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:34.250
I know we all hate to hear
this, but we don't know.

00:24:34.250 --> 00:24:35.520
The evidence I've laid out here

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:37.600
for both the lab leak hypothesis,

00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:41.690
as well as the spillover
hypothesis is all circumstantial

00:24:41.690 --> 00:24:44.270
meaning, it's like you have
to connect a lot of dots

00:24:44.270 --> 00:24:45.150
to make it work.

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:47.230
And science isn't about connecting dots,

00:24:47.230 --> 00:24:50.740
it's about proving something
with solid evidence.

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:52.960
We don't have solid proof of anything.

00:24:52.960 --> 00:24:56.890
So please, please, please
don't give into the temptation

00:24:56.890 --> 00:24:59.390
to now believe that COVID came from a lab.

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:01.670
It may have come from a lab

00:25:01.670 --> 00:25:04.300
but it may have jumped from animals

00:25:04.300 --> 00:25:07.370
after being infected from
bats, we do not know,

00:25:07.370 --> 00:25:08.670
we should investigate both.

00:25:08.670 --> 00:25:11.470
Number two, it is mind blowing to me

00:25:11.470 --> 00:25:14.220
that a hypothesis can be labeled as fringe

00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:18.370
and conspiracy all because of politics.

00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:21.300
And then it can just
immediately get reversed

00:25:21.300 --> 00:25:23.910
depending on the political climate.

00:25:23.910 --> 00:25:27.840
The media so hardcore
downplayed the hypothesis

00:25:27.840 --> 00:25:30.590
of the lab leak and they did
so because Trump was in office

00:25:30.590 --> 00:25:32.810
and he was using an
overstated version of that

00:25:32.810 --> 00:25:35.350
to stoke hate and tension and lies.

00:25:35.350 --> 00:25:38.470
So I kind of get it but we
sort of threw the baby out

00:25:38.470 --> 00:25:39.420
with the bath water.

00:25:39.420 --> 00:25:42.220
Number three, it is
very disappointing to me

00:25:42.220 --> 00:25:44.990
that scientists whose
motives should be nothing

00:25:44.990 --> 00:25:48.040
but seeking the truth, keeping
everything on the table

00:25:48.040 --> 00:25:50.640
that has any promise, they
are digging in their heels,

00:25:50.640 --> 00:25:53.330
throwing a legitimate
hypothesis off the table

00:25:53.330 --> 00:25:55.300
and lobbying to keep it out of the public

00:25:55.300 --> 00:25:57.300
and showing that they're
probably influenced

00:25:57.300 --> 00:25:59.240
by the fact that their funding

00:25:59.240 --> 00:26:02.410
and life's work is associated
with the other hypothesis

00:26:02.410 --> 00:26:03.243
that they don't like.

00:26:03.243 --> 00:26:04.930
I get it when politicians do that

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:08.150
but leading experts who were
all looking to for truth

00:26:08.150 --> 00:26:10.330
and guidance, like, come on guys,

00:26:10.330 --> 00:26:13.190
we need to stay open to any hypothesis

00:26:13.190 --> 00:26:15.770
that has a reasonable basis to stand on

00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:17.610
and we need to do that so we can find out

00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:19.260
how this thing started

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:22.260
and ensure that it never happens again.

00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:24.030
- A final note, more than a year ago,

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:25.610
top scientists published a letter

00:26:25.610 --> 00:26:27.660
in the prestigious medical journal, Lancet

00:26:27.660 --> 00:26:29.240
that dismissed the lab leak theory,

00:26:29.240 --> 00:26:30.997
they called a conspiracy theory.

00:26:30.997 --> 00:26:33.830
So ABC news reached out
to all 27 scientists

00:26:33.830 --> 00:26:36.350
who signed that letter
about a dozen responded,

00:26:36.350 --> 00:26:37.370
several of them telling us,

00:26:37.370 --> 00:26:39.640
they're not so sure this
thing came from nature

00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:42.800
and one scientist is telling
us he's flipped entirely

00:26:42.800 --> 00:26:46.743
and he believes it now the lab
leak theory is more likely.

00:26:46.743 --> 00:26:49.493
(beat box music)

